course: dictionary
lesson: 717
title: Barley, a crop from the field
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Barley is a cereal plant, like wheat and oats. Farmers grow it in fields, and its grain is used for food, for animal feed, and for making beer and malt. «Piles of wheat, oats, barley, beech-mast and nuts lie ready to be moved.» The list tells you barley belongs with other grains that are grown and stored.
explain: Look for clues in the words near a new word. In «Alice's new rule: pepper makes people hot-tempered, vinegar sour, camomile bitter, and barley-sugar (a hard sweet) makes children sweet-tempered», the brackets explain that barley-sugar is a hard sweet. The word barley is hidden inside it, so barley-sugar is a sweet made with barley.
explain: Barley is a noun that we do not count, so we say barley, not barleys. You can have a field of barley, barley water or pearl barley. Barley sounds a little like barely, which means only just, but the two words are different, so check the sentence before you decide.
fact: Barley is a cereal plant, and its grain is used for food, for animal feed, and for making beer and malt.
fact: In history, barley was one of the first crops people grew.
fact: «In autumn farmers plough and sow winter wheat or barley, and gulls and rooks follow the plough to snatch worms and grubs.»
fact: Barley-sugar is a hard sweet, and barley water is a drink from the UK.
fact: Barley is uncountable, so it has no plural: we say some barley, not two barleys.
exercise: «In autumn farmers plough and sow winter wheat or barley.» What is barley? | *A cereal plant grown on farms for its grain | A kind of sweet eaten at Christmas | A tool for digging the soil | A bird that follows the plough
exercise: Alice's rule says barley-sugar makes children sweet-tempered. What is barley-sugar? | A grey stone found in fields | *A hard sweet | A type of tractor used on farms | A bird that eats worms
exercise: Which of these is a food made from barley? | *Barley soup | Camomile | Pepper | Vinegar
test: «Sleep takes him as a swathe of barley is folded into the arms of the reaping machine.» What is the swathe of barley? | *A row of barley plants being gathered | A cut bunch of barley crop, lying in a line | A bag of flour for baking bread | A wooden box for holding sweets
test: Which word would NOT be a type of grain? | Wheat | *Gulls | Oats | Barley
exam: Piles of «wheat, oats, barley, beech-mast and nuts» lie ready to be moved; in this list, what does barley belong with? | Tools for ploughing the soil | Animals like gulls and rooks | *Other grains such as wheat and oats | Sweets like barley-sugar
